\ Two opaque operands a `swap` left in descending slot order, feeding the
\ polymorphic arithmetic path. The cold arm reads both operands off the physical
\ stack and sets SP from the second slot alone, so an unsettled pair points it
\ below the operands. Padding keeps `sub2` past the splice threshold so the call
\ site really calls it.
\
\ The overflow drives the pair into the cold arm, where the fixnum entry
\ promotes; a misaddressed pair reports a dispatch miss or a stack underflow
\ instead.

kind: generic ( x -- s ) [ drop "other" ] ;
kind: method{ fixnum } [ drop "fixnum" ] ;
kind: method{ bignum } [ drop "bignum" ] ;

sub2: ( a b -- r ) [ swap 0 drop 0 drop 0 drop 0 drop 0 drop 0 drop - ] ;

pick-huge: ( b -- n ) [ [ 9223372036854775807 ] [ 2.5 ] if ] ;

t pick-huge -9223372036854775807 sub2 kind print-line
